## The seam between the vanilla fluid code (worldadapter.runTickData) and the finite-fluid host (src/server/fluids/fluidhost.aowl).
## This file imports NOTHING, so worldadapter can import it without a cycle. With the finite fluids OFF (the default) the flag is
## false and the only cost anywhere is one bool test per fluid tick: vanilla water and lava behave exactly as before.

var gFluidTicksSuppressed*: bool = false
  ## true while the finite-fluid host owns the fluids: the scheduled and random fluid ticks of vanilla water and lava are skipped
  ## (they would spread blocks the conserved model does not know about).
